        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Here  and  are obtained from the surrounding points by simple linear interpolation."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 13864,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 569,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 227,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Due to the incompressible flow assumption the dynamic pressure does not have a separate time evolution equation, but instead it satisfies an elliptical equation in space. As such its effect cannot be calculated explicitly using values at the previous time level. However to improve the accuracy of the predictor step the effect of the dynamic pressure is included explicitly. To do this first the unknown pressure is decomposed as:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 13915,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 571,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 229,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "where the difference in pressure is generally small. In the predictor step the effect of the pressure is included explicitly using. In the corrector step the full Poisson equation is then solved for . The pressure term in the predictor step is thus given as"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
